<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Federation of Arab Emirates of the South</h1><p class="st-meta">1959 CE – 1962 CE · capital Al Ittihad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British-sponsored union of protected states in the Aden hinterland, created in 1959 to secure Britain's base at Aden.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Facing Arab nationalism and claims by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mutawakkilite-kingdom-of-yemen">Mutawakkilite Kingdom of Yemen</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> encouraged the rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Western Aden Protectorate</a> to federate. On 11 February 1959 six states, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/audhali-sultanate">Audhali Sultanate</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-beihan">Emirate of Beihan</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-dhala">Emirate of Dhala</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fadhli-sultanate">Fadhli Sultanate</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lower-yafa-sultanate">Lower Yafa Sultanate</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/upper-aulaqi-sheikhdom">Upper Aulaqi Sheikhdom</a>, signed the federation treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federation had a supreme council of rulers and a federal government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madinat-ash-shab">Al Ittihad</a>, a new capital built near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> kept responsibility for defence and foreign affairs and provided aid and the Federal Regular Army. Other states, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-lahej">Sultanate of Lahej</a>, joined in the following years.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In April 1962 the federation was renamed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a>, in preparation for the entry of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-aden">Colony of Aden</a> in 1963.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south.jpg" alt="Federation of Arab Emirates of the South" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Federation_of_South_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1959 CE – 1962 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Al Ittihad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federation of the Emirates of the South</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south" aria-label="Federation of Arab Emirates of the South on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5993 1607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Federation of Arab Emirates of the South lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6313 1863L4997 651M6313 1863L6313 1863M6313 1863L6247 1946M6313 1863L6252 1934M6313 1863L6256 1915M6313 1863L6252 1934M6313 1863L6226 1924M6313 1863L6273 1938M6313 1863L6242 1941M6313 1863L6222 1967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M6313 1863h0M6247 1946h0M6252 1934h0M6256 1915h0M6252 1934h0M6226 1924h0M6273 1938h0M6242 1941h0M6222 1967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6313 1863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6313 1863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
